summary:
Cycle 8.
The screenshots are published (editor-views satisfied).
The generic cull took draws from about 700 to 200–323 per frame, though it threw on a scene child with a null userData, so plays-clean is contradicted. The frame ratio reads 4.76 on this software renderer's noisy clock.
The guest's trail shows a clean climb out of the water to the ladder's top (-404, onLadder 1). The probe then judged 'not on the cap' from ch.y + 44, which is wrong for a landing pose: the guest was at x 2488, over the cap.
The solo water test began 47 px off the ladder, outside its 28 px catch.
The detail grid is 0.061 against 0.06. The furniture didn't show: it was placed behind the rooms' back walls (z about -45..-25).
The five-way read-only review (a workflow of reviewers, each finding checked by a refuting skeptic) confirmed these defects:
- checkpoints light by x alone;
- the lit-berth replacement is dead code;
- a patrol with a live gunner can pass as the players' boat;
- a stale ladder clock;
- restoring culled meshes via visible can undo the engine's own hiding;
- state.level is sticky;
- the exit lock isn't synced to guests;
- probes run with the editor's Shadows OFF, so none of the level's lamps are baked into what's measured.
